    "captions": [
      {
        "t": 0,
        "text": "Dawn, 17 January 1781. Tarleton's 1,100 men have marched since 2 a.m. Morgan waits in three lines on an open cattle pasture, with a flooded river miles behind him, so his militia cannot run far."
      },
      {
        "t": 4,
        "text": "Tarleton forms up at once and advances. Picked riflemen out in front aim at officers, then fall back on the militia line."
      },
      {
        "t": 11,
        "text": "Pickens's militia hold their fire until the British are close, fire the two volleys Morgan asked of them, then file off round the American left."
      },
      {
        "t": 15,
        "text": "The 17th Light Dragoons charge the retreating militia. Washington's cavalry sweeps out from behind the rise and drives them off."
      },
      {
        "t": 20,
        "text": "The British line, thinned by the militia volleys, meets Howard's Continentals on the crest. The 71st Highlanders come up on the left to overlap the American right."
      },
      {
        "t": 26,
        "text": "Howard orders his right-hand company to turn and face the Highlanders. It mishears and falls back, and the whole line follows, in good order."
      },
      {
        "t": 29.5,
        "text": "The British think the Americans are beaten and rush forward, losing their formation. Morgan rides up and shows Howard where to halt."
      },
      {"t": 31, "text": "The Continentals turn about, fire a volley at about 30 yards and charge with the bayonet."},
      {
        "t": 33.5,
        "text": "Washington's cavalry strikes the British right. Pickens's militia, rallied behind the hill, come round to hit the Highlanders on the left. Tarleton's infantry is surrounded."
      },
      {
        "t": 37,
        "text": "Most of the British infantry throw down their arms. Tarleton's reserve of about 200 Legion horsemen refuses to charge and rides away."
      },
      {
        "t": 41,
        "text": "Tarleton escapes with a few dozen men after a sword fight with William Washington. In under an hour he has lost almost his whole force."
      }
    ],
